{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/sourceprotocol\/isdestroyed"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/SourceProtocol"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/SourceProtocol\/isDestroyed"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"Returns whether ","type":"text"},{"code":"source","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has been destroyed.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isDestroyed","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol","extendedModule":"GLib","modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","externalID":"s:4GLib14SourceProtocolPAAE11isDestroyedSbvp","title":"isDestroyed"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isDestroyed","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":" { "},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is important when you operate upon your objects"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from within idle handlers, but may have freed the object"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"before the dispatch of your idle handler."}]},{"code":["static gboolean","idle_callback (gpointer data)","{","  SomeWidget *self = data;","   ","  g_mutex_lock (&self->idle_id_mutex);","  \/\/ do stuff with self","  self->idle_id = 0;","  g_mutex_unlock (&self->idle_id_mutex);","   ","  return G_SOURCE_REMOVE;","}"," ","static void","some_widget_do_stuff_later (SomeWidget *self)","{","  g_mutex_lock (&self->idle_id_mutex);","  self->idle_id = g_idle_add (idle_callback, self);","  g_mutex_unlock (&self->idle_id_mutex);","}"," ","static void","some_widget_init (SomeWidget *self)","{","  g_mutex_init (&self->idle_id_mutex);","","  \/\/ ...","}","","static void","some_widget_finalize (GObject *object)","{","  SomeWidget *self = SOME_WIDGET (object);","   ","  if (self->idle_id)","    g_source_remove (self->idle_id);","   ","  g_mutex_clear (&self->idle_id_mutex);","","  G_OBJECT_CLASS (parent_class)->finalize (object);","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"c"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This will fail in a multi-threaded application if the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"widget is destroyed before the idle handler fires due"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"to the use after free in the callback. A solution, to","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this particular problem, is to check to if the source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has already been destroy within the callback."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"c","code":["static gboolean","idle_callback (gpointer data)","{","  SomeWidget *self = data;","  ","  g_mutex_lock (&self->idle_id_mutex);","  if (!g_source_is_destroyed (g_main_current_source ()))","    {","      \/\/ do stuff with self","    }","  g_mutex_unlock (&self->idle_id_mutex);","  ","  return FALSE;","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Calls to this function from a thread other than the one acquired by the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"[struct","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MainContext","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"] the [struct"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Source","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"] is attached to are typically","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"redundant, as the source could be destroyed immediately after this function","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returns. However, once a source is destroyed it cannot be un-destroyed, so"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this function can be used for opportunistic checks from any thread.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/Source":{"url":"\/documentation\/glib\/source","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GSource"},{"text":" struct is an opaque data type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"representing an event source.","type":"text"}],"title":"Source","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Source"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Source","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Source"}]},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/MainContext":{"title":"MainContext","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MainContext","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MainContext"}],"url":"\/documentation\/glib\/maincontext","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MainContext"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"GMainContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" struct is an opaque data","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"type representing a set of sources to be handled in a main loop."}]},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib","title":"GLib","abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/glib","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/SourceProtocol":{"navi